{"assets":["/statement-assets/a51911911c7329260879e7bfbf9c472ee5c8929cd0c12540a8268755c82d2f33.png","/statement-assets/e8b4730ea23f6b7661ab72e8578972639a38bf082de40636e381afcb486fce57.png","/statement-assets/707be16df301ff6f521f3e5b9b358ea2d5405647953edfe59f9c33baca6ddc7f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1299","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Aerodynamic"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Guy-Manuel and Thomas are going to build a polygon spaceship."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You're given a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strictly convex"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (i. e. no three points are collinear) polygon $$$P$$$ which is defined by coordinates of its vertices. Define $$$P(x,y)$$$ as a polygon obtained by translating $$$P$$$ by vector $$$\\overrightarrow {(x,y)}$$$. The picture below depicts an example of the translation:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/a51911911c7329260879e7bfbf9c472ee5c8929cd0c12540a8268755c82d2f33.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Define $$$T$$$ as a set of points which is the union of all $$$P(x,y)$$$ such that the origin $$$(0,0)$$$ lies in $$$P(x,y)$$$ (both strictly inside and on the boundary). There is also an equivalent definition: a point $$$(x,y)$$$ lies in $$$T$$$ only if there are two points $$$A,B$$$ in $$$P$$$ such that $$$\\overrightarrow {AB} = \\overrightarrow {(x,y)}$$$. One can prove $$$T$$$ is a polygon too. For example, if $$$P$$$ is a regular triangle then $$$T$$$ is a regular hexagon. At the picture below $$$P$$$ is drawn in black and some $$$P(x,y)$$$ which contain the origin are drawn in colored: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e8b4730ea23f6b7661ab72e8578972639a38bf082de40636e381afcb486fce57.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The spaceship has the best aerodynamic performance if $$$P$$$ and $$$T$$$ are similar."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Your task is to check whether the polygons $$$P$$$ and $$$T$$$ are "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://tinyurl.com/vp5m7vl"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"similar"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input will contain a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of points."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The $$$i$$$-th of the next $$$n$$$ lines contains two integers $$$x_i, y_i$$$ ($$$|x_i|, |y_i| \\le 10^9$$$), denoting the coordinates of the $$$i$$$-th vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that these points are listed in counterclockwise order and these points form a strictly convex polygon."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"YES\""}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in a separate line, if $$$P$$$ and $$$T$$$ are similar. Otherwise, output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"NO\""}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in a separate line. You can print each letter in any case (upper or lower)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 0\n4 1\n3 4\n0 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n100 86\n50 0\n150 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nnO"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n0 0\n1 0\n2 1\n3 3\n4 6\n3 6\n2 5\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following image shows the first sample: both $$$P$$$ and $$$T$$$ are squares. The second sample was shown in the statements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/707be16df301ff6f521f3e5b9b358ea2d5405647953edfe59f9c33baca6ddc7f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1299B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1299/problem/B"}